<!--
  Pip, Claude Code Quest's mascot: one artboard holding the art, the state
  machine and its timelines (RML keeps an artboard's timelines and state
  machine inside its own element, so they share this file). The view model,
  its enum and the converters are in view-model.rml.

  Built only by `npm run pip:build` with the pinned Rive CLI. Script-free: no
  Luau, ever.

  The art is the approved board's three-quarter view, traced in an 800-unit
  reference space inside the root node, which scales it onto the 400 by 400
  artboard. Each moving part pivots at its own node: the neck (Head, Head Pose),
  the shoulders (Arm Left, Arm Right), the stalk bases (Antenna Left, Antenna
  Right), the soles (Foot Left, Foot Right), Hop for the whole body's lift and
  squash, and the outer edge of each sole for its lean (Lean Left, Lean Right),
  so a lean keeps a foot on the floor. Soft shading is feathered fills clipped
  to the part they shade.

  Two rules bind every timeline:
  - each Body timeline keys the whole rest pose, so any state blends back to it
    without a jump;
  - a blend state's exit names the timeline that times it (exitBlendAnimationId).
  The Blink layer alone keys the eyes' height (a later layer wins), so the
  Reactions show surprise through the mouth and the body, never the eyes.
-->
<Rive version="1" kind="fragment">
    <Artboard defaultStateMachineId="0:7" styleId="0:5" viewModelId="0:40" viewModelInstanceId="0:42" width="400" height="400" name="Pip" id="0:2">
        <LayoutComponentStyle name="Artboard Style" id="0:5"/>

        <!-- Pip faces right, toward the content: the root mirrors the board's
             three-quarter view (scaleX negative, x moved to the far edge), so the
             gaze converters in view-model.rml map +x the other way. The scale and
             position stand Pip on the artboard's floor with room above for the
             highest hop: the artboard clips what it draws, so the frame holds
             every Reaction at full intensity (e2e/pip-contract.spec.ts checks). -->
        <Node x="375.6" y="45.4" scaleX="-0.44" scaleY="0.44" name="Pip" id="0:100">

            <Node x="405" y="765" name="Hop" id="0:101">
                <!-- The lean: each pivot sits at the centre of the rounded outer
                     corner of one foot's sole, so Pip rocks onto the foot it leans
                     toward, which stays on the floor, and the other foot lifts. Lean
                     Left takes rotations of 0 and below, Lean Right 0 and above. -->
                <Node x="-141" y="-11" name="Lean Left" id="0:103">
                    <Node x="282" y="0" name="Lean Right" id="0:104">
                        <Node x="-546" y="-754" name="Body Art" id="0:102">

